<article class="env-corollary" id="06AX">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06AX">Corollary <span data-tag="06AX">7.3.8.2</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a simplicial set, and let $\overline{F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a diagram. Assume that, for each vertex $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the image $\overline{F}(C)$ is a $U$-initial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. Then $\overline{F}$ is a $U$-colimit diagram if and only if it carries the cone point of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright }$ to a $U$-initial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a data-tag="01BQ" href="/tag/01BQ">4.1.3.3</a>, we can choose an inner anodyne map $\iota : \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$ where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$ is an $\infty $-category. Since $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is an $\infty $-category, we can extend $\overline{F}$ to a functor $\overline{F}': \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. By virtue of Corollary <a data-tag="02XQ" href="/tag/02XQ">7.2.2.2</a>, we can replace $\overline{F}$ by $\overline{F}'$ and thereby reduce to proving Corollary <a data-tag="06AX" href="/tag/06AX">7.3.8.2</a> in the special case where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an $\infty $-category. This follows from Proposition <a data-tag="030V" href="/tag/030V">7.3.8.1</a>, applied in the special case where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0} = \emptyset $ (see Example <a data-tag="043F" href="/tag/043F">7.3.3.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
